5e93dc98ed%2Fap26296421881981.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3825x2152+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F33%2Fa9%2F06089dc548abaaae295e93dc98ed%2Fap26296421881981.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3825x2152+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F33%2Fa9%2F06089dc548abaaae295e93dc98ed%2Fap26296421881981.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3825x2152+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F33%2Fa9%2F06089dc548abaaae295e93dc98ed%2Fap26296421881981.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3825x2152+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F33%2Fa9%2F06089dc548abaaae295e93dc98ed%2Fap26296421881981.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3825x2152+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F33%2Fa9%2F06089dc548abaaae295e93dc98ed%2Fap26296421881981.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3825x2152+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F33%2Fa9%2F06089dc548abaaae295e93dc98ed%2Fap26296421881981.jpg" class="img" alt="Pilgrims pray in front of the Kaaba, Islam&amp;#039;s holiest shrine, at the Grand Mosque in Mecca, Saudi Arabia. Muslims will outnumber Christians by 2070, according to a new report." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Pilgrims pray in front of the Kaaba, Islam's holiest shrine, at the Grand Mosque in Mecca, Saudi Arabia. Muslims will outnumber Christians by 2070, according to a new report.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          STR/AP                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ol class="edTag rte2-style-ol"&gt;&lt;li&gt;A new Pew Research Center report shows that by 2035, Muslims will become the &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/19/nx-s1-6043018/muslims-will-outnumber-christians-worldwide-by-2070-report-says" target="_blank"&gt;largest religious group globally&lt;/a&gt;, surpassing Christians.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The Cincinnati Zoo &amp; Botanical Garden announced that Fiona, the famous 9-year-old hippo, has died after &lt;a href="https://www.wvxu.org/local-news/2026-11-19/beloved-cincinnati-zoo-hippo-fiona-has-died?utm_source=npr.org&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=national_highlight&amp;utm_content=homepage" target="_blank"&gt;failing to pass a hat&lt;/a&gt; she ingested more than a week ago. (via &lt;a href="https://www.wvxu.org/" target="_blank"&gt;WVXU&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Mayor Zohran Mamdani &lt;a href="https://gothamist.com/news/mayor-mamdani-signs-nycs-carriage-horse-ban-after-decades-of-animal-rights-activism" target="_blank"&gt;signed a bill yesterday banning&lt;/a&gt; New York City's 160-year-old horse-drawn carriage industry. Animal rights activists have fought for decades to end the practice. (via &lt;a href="https://gothamist.com/" target="_blank"&gt;Gothamist&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This newsletter was edited by &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/859721331/suzanne-nuyen"target="_blank"   &gt;&lt;em&gt;Suzanne Nuyen&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
